## 9. Regression baseline and root cause

Packet 001 attribution lane, the observation Task 239 exists to explain
(`001/.../attribution-run/attribution/distann-local-multinode.log:24`):

    materialization correctness scenario exactly_one_window failed:
      rows=10/10 identity=true null_ok=true external_toast_ok=true
      remote_requested=8 local_consumed=4 payload_reads=12/10 duplicate_requested=0

Root cause is visible in the ported hunk `git show 21c013079`:

    -    if variant.materialization_batch_size != 10 {
    -        ... "SET ec_distann.benchmark_materialization_batch_size = {}" ...
    +        "SET ec_distann.benchmark_materialization_batch_size = {}",
    +        variant.materialization_batch_size

A variant at batch size 10 previously emitted no `SET`, so in the shared
attribution session the "lazy-10" candidate inherited the eager control's 0 and
the measured arm was not the production policy. The port also reads the value
back with `current_setting(..., true)` per arm and fails closed if absent, which
is what the `control_batch_size=0 candidate_batch_size=10` fields on every core
row now attest.

